  "plot_summary": "(The Doctor Strange tale opens with a note saying that Marvel was waiting to hear back from readers about whether they wanted more of the character.&nbsp; Apparently the answer was a resounding yes, so here is the 3<sup>rd</sup> installment...)\n\nBaron Mordo, disguised as an old friend of Strange, a \"Sir Clive Bentley,\" calls for help.&nbsp; Strange arrives at Bentley's castle (in London we soon find out) to find it apparently deserted.&nbsp; But the fumes of a candle paralyze him as Mordo appears to remind him that after the Ancient One is gone, there will only be one Master of the Mystic Arts.&nbsp; They were both taught by him, but it will be Mordo that steps up to take his place when he is finally gone!&nbsp; Strange will die once the candle burns itself out!\n\nStrange projects his thoughts out to the nearest human, a girl in a nearby country home is compelled to snuff out the candle.&nbsp; Turns out the girl has a latent power of sorcery herself, and she's the daughter of Lord Bentley, who died ten years earlier!&nbsp; When Mordo returns to gloat, he finds Strange free and tries to take over his mind, but only then do we learn that this isn't Strange after all but a mental projection, for how could he have arrived from the United States so quickly otherwise - his <i>real</i> self is just now arriving by jet plane.\n\nThey battle mentally until Mordo is driven back, but Strange knows he will be back.&nbsp; Victoria Bentley is not yet ready to become Strange's disciple.&nbsp; The Ancient One watches from afar.\n\nWe're promised that the series will kick into high gear next issue.",
